+## Proactive sends — persona-initiated outreach (card line-proactive-persona)
+
+Replies answer a turn; a **proactive** send starts one. The backend
+tool (`chat_send`) declares `intent='proactive'` and the relay owns the
+policy — a persona can engage a member without being spoken to, e.g.
+kaewta pings nhong about the kk car photo she just served Tony.
+
+- **Member DM:** `chat_send(to='nhong', intent='proactive', ...)` —
+  `to=` resolves a display name / caller / alias / member-directory /
+  mddb-registry hit to a userId, so `nhong` lands in her DM with the
+  bot. (`to='owner'` still aliases the relay owner.)
+- **In-group ping:** `chat_send(mention='nhong', text=...)` — the relay
+  prepends `@<displayName>` (per-member group profile endpoint) and
+  attaches LINE's `mention` object, so the member's LINE actually
+  pings. `mention=` needs a group/room target — bare `to=` unset means
+  the chat the turn came from.
+- **Policy (relay-enforced):** `intent='proactive'` is honored only
+  when the sending `instance` sits in `LINE_PROACTIVE_ALLOW` — the
+  backend-declared-intent gate; unset env denies every proactive send.
+  Per (instance, chat) and per (instance, member) debounce
+  `LINE_PROACTIVE_DEBOUNCE_S` (600s), per (instance, chat) day cap
+  `LINE_PROACTIVE_DAY_CAP` (8); state write-through to
+  `LINE_PROACTIVE_STATE` so restarts don't reset. Denials answer
+  403/429 with `{ok:false}` — the backend surfaces it to the model, so
+  a persona cannot "sent it anyway" narrate.
+- **Owner-tier on the tool side:** a secondary (identified guest) turn
+  can't declare `intent='proactive'`, `mention=`, or `to=<other chat>`
+  — `PermissionError` at the gate. Member lanes keep their
+  `LINE_LANE_ALLOW` ceiling regardless.
+- **Member directory:** `LINE_MEMBER_NAMES` persists
+  userId→displayName learned from profile fetches/registry writes so
+  name resolution survives restarts; the mddb registry scan
+  (`LINE_REGISTRY_LOOKUP_TTL_S`, 300s) covers members the file
+  predates.
+- Audit: `proactive_sent` / `proactive_denied` / `proactive_debounced`
+  / `mention_failed` ops events + `proactive_msgs` in the send ledger
+  rollup.
+
